6838903","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112184#issuecomment-3476838903","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112184","id":3476838903,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7PPFn3","user":{"login":"Ryan-000","id":73148864,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczMTQ4ODY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73148864?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000","html_url":"https://github.com/Ryan-000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-01T20:57:05Z","updated_at":"2025-11-01T20:57:05Z","body":"\r\n> difference between local and world coordinate, how does it behave in those cases\r\n\r\nLocal coordinates: changing scale rescales the entire simulation, including existing particles.  \r\nWorld coordinates: changing scale only affects particles spawned after the change.\r\n\r\n> does it create issues with trails\r\n\r\nNo. but enabling it fixes a bug. In world coordinates, `GPUParticle3D.scale` previously changed motion, but not the trail mesh scale. Now the mesh scales too. Local space already behaved correctly.\r\n\r\n> what happens if the emitter is scaled in an animation\r\n\r\nWorks as expected. Behaviour is determined by `GPUParticle3D.local_coords`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godo